{"name":"Lovestruck","hex":"#6a2e36","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lovestruck","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of love-struck."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lovestruck"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lovestruck (Madness song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lovestruck\" is a song by the English ska and pop band Madness, released as the lead single from their seventh studio album, Wonderful (1999), on 19 July 1999. This release marked the first time Madness had put out original material for over 10 years and signified their return to music. \"Lovestruck\" peaked at number 10 on the UK singles chart, which was the first time a new Madness release had reached the top 10 since the 1983 release \"The Sun and the Rain\". The song also charted in Iceland, reaching number 36 on the Íslenski Listinn Topp 40."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/8b/Madness_-_Lovestruck.jpg/330px-Madness_-_Lovestruck.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovestruck_(Madness_song)","wikidata":"Q15531561"},{"title":"Lovestruck (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Lovestruck is a 2005 Philippine romantic comedy film directed by Louie Ignacio. The film stars Jolina Magdangal, Jennylyn Mercado, Mark Herras and Mike Tan."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovestruck_(film)","wikidata":"Q108365654"},{"title":"Falling in love","blocks":[{"text":"Falling in love is the development of strong feelings of attachment and love, usually towards another person."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Albert_Schr%C3%B6der_Musikalische_Unterhaltung_1885.jpg/330px-Albert_Schr%C3%B6der_Musikalische_Unterhaltung_1885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Falling_in_love","wikidata":"Q1854755"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Leighton-God_Speed%21.jpg/500px-Leighton-God_Speed%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Leighton-God_Speed%21.jpg/1280px-Leighton-God_Speed%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Leighton-God_Speed%21.jpg/500px-Leighton-God_Speed%21.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"God Speed by English artist Edmund Leighton, 1900: depicting an armored knight departing for war and leaving behind his lover","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeighton-God_Speed!.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Jean-Honor%C3%A9_Fragonard_-_The_Stolen_Kiss.jpg/500px-Jean-Honor%C3%A9_Fragonard_-_The_Stolen_Kiss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Jean-Honor%C3%A9_Fragonard_-_The_Stolen_Kiss.jpg/1280px-Jean-Honor%C3%A9_Fragonard_-_The_Stolen_Kiss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Jean-Honor%C3%A9_Fragonard_-_The_Stolen_Kiss.jpg/500px-Jean-Honor%C3%A9_Fragonard_-_The_Stolen_Kiss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Jean-Honoré Fragonard—The Stolen Kiss (circa late 1780s)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJean-Honor%C3%A9_Fragonard_-_The_Stolen_Kiss.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png/500px-Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png/500px-Mesocorticolimbic_Circuit.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=par